# The design (the SoC with the pipelined core, design/pipe/core.sv), in
# required compile order. One path per line, relative to the repo root.
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored. Never add a verification/taxi/-touching
# file here -- that tree is Verilator-only and will not compile under Icarus.
#
# decoder.sv comes first: it defines INSTR_CODE, which qv_decode.sv uses, and
# qv_pkg.sv comes before every module that imports it. The tools that need only
# the core's own files (lockstep, the RVFI diff, ACT, the formal sync, the Sail
# diff) take them from this list with
#   grep -E '^design/(pipe/|decoder\.sv|alu\.sv|c_expand\.sv|csr_file\.sv|register_file\.sv|divider\.sv)'
# so a new module is added here and nowhere else. The frozen multi-cycle
# reference has its own list, ref_design_files.list.
design/decoder.sv
design/alu.sv
design/c_expand.sv
design/cache_complex.sv
design/clint.sv
design/pipe/qv_pkg.sv
design/pipe/qv_fetch.sv
design/pipe/qv_align.sv
design/pipe/qv_fifo.sv
design/pipe/qv_btb.sv
design/pipe/qv_ras.sv
